Overview
This practical implements a Convolutional Neural Network (CNN) for classifying potato leaf images into different disease categories. 
The model is trained using the Potato Disease dataset and evaluated using accuracy, precision, recall, F1-score, and a confusion matrix.

Dataset – Potato Disease
The Potato Disease dataset contains 2,152 images of potato leaves divided into three classes:
Early Blight
Late Blight
Healthy
The images are resized to 128 × 128 pixels and processed as RGB images with 3 channels.

CNN Model
The CNN consists of:
Three convolutional layers with 32, 64, and 128 filters.
Max-pooling layers after each convolutional layer.
Flatten layer.
Dense layer with 128 neurons and ReLU activation.
Dropout layer with a rate of 0.5.
Output layer using Softmax for classification.
The model uses the Adam optimizer and Sparse Categorical Crossentropy loss.
